  "description": "XEVPEX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C134 H100 Cl10 Dy8 N10 O44,6(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.510-3.978 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.63-113.77°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy8(ov5ca)6(a5ca)4(ov)2(μ-OH)6]·6CH3OH (EA: C140H118Cl10Dy8N10O50).",
